WEBVTT

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.560
Why don't you just calm down?!

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.880
It's annoying with you pacing around like a bear.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:23.830
Even you, Pops—

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.470
P-Pops.  Pops!

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.700
This is Garage Hill.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.710
Oh, thank you.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:36.630
Yes.  Yes.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.940
Yes.  Yes.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.030
Yes.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.200
Thank you very much.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.870
If you'll excuse me.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.450
P-Pops?

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.480
You passed!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.670
You got through to the final selection for the FSRS!

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.820
W-What?!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.550
Don't scare me like that, Pops!

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.670
All right, it's here!

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.540
I'll get that scholarship!

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.460
All right!

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.800
You just wait, Minamoto!

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.650
Shige-san, you have a phone call.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.720
Okay.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.410
Yes, this is Taira.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.190
Oh, Oka-san.  Hello.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.320
Thank you very much for back then.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.150
How is your work?

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.150
Well, thanks to his racing,
 I'm poor and have no time to rest.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.120
<b>Why?</b>

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:30.010
The thing is, our Ryou has gone through to the FSRS final selection.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.660
<b>Oh, so you, too.</b>

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.620
Eh?  "You, too"?

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.150
What a coincidence.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.590
Our Capeta also got through.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.830
Yes...

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:39.660
Yes.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.600
That's it...

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.800
Ah, yes.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.630
Yes, that's right.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.620
If you'll excuse me.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.590
Bye.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.470
<i>You did it, Capeta.</i>

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.300
<i>Now it's your dad's turn.</i>

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.490
Shige-san!

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.290
Let's raise our glasses to celebrate Capeta-kun's success in getting through to the final selection!

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.640
I'll be right there!

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.440
Taira-kun also got through...

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.410
Taira.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.460
Summer break is over.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.050
And so many of you haven't decided on your choice of schools.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.260
You're all slacking off!

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.260
Geez!

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.600
Don't stay in summer break mode forever.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.580
Understand?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.610
That's how it is,

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:02.980
so please discuss your choice of schools with your parents before the next parent-teacher meeting.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.410
Understand?

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.980
Yes.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.410
Uh... Uh... Ummm...

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.980
What is it, Shige?

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.620
Don't you still have a job to finish?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.350
Hurry up and—

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.010
Um, Boss...

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.050
If you will please.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.720
What is this?

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.940
I-I'm resigning for personal reasons.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.050
What do you mean, "personal reasons"?

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.770
This is about the charge for that car Capeta wrecked, right?

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.100
Y-Yes.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.050
And how much is it?

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:49.740
1-1,650,000 yen.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.860
1-1,650,000 yen.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:56.580
And how are you thinking of paying it off after you quit work?

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.190
I-I was thinking of going for migrant work.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.790
Maybe the Atlantic or the Indian Ocean.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.550
You...

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.080
Don't you also have a debt to this company?!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.750
Yes... that's...

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.180
Like I'm gonna let you run off.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.340
You're going to work here for the rest of your life!

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.860
B-But there's Capeta's debt...

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.060
I have to get the money or we'll be in trouble!

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.520
I'll pay for it.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.720
Shige-san!  You won't have to go on the boat!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.610
Th-Thank you very much!

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.490
Yes...

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.180
But if you could somehow...

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.460
Yes.  It is but...

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.910
I understand...

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:44.790
Yes.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.250
If you'll excuse me.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.580
But still, I can't believe you got through to the final selection.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.600
I thought you failed.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.720
Me, too.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.330
Not only did I crash,

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:05.140
but I also lost to Shiba.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:11.640
At one stage, I thought that I wouldn't lose as long as the conditions were the same.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.220
Capeta.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.730
What are you doing with a sad face?

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.680
Monami.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.220
Ca-chan, you did it!

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:21.060
I'm going to come and cheer you on, okay?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.110
Th-Thanks.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.660
What?

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:29.640
You got through to the final selection, so why don't you look more cheerful!

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.100
Hey, Capeta.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.200
I'll make sure you get to practice on a formula machine this time.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:38.930
Formula?  Where will we be able to drive one?

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.030
Tada!  Look at this!

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:49.020
I've picked up every place that might lend us a machine.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:51.810
Nobu.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.780
With this many, one of them is bound to lend us a machine.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.900
Listen.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:03.950
Ca-chan had to do the audition on the spot because of you, Nobu, okay?

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.230
W-What?!

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.450
Why is your attitude always this big?

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.500
Because I'm the manager of Team Capeta.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.990
Right.  Right.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.360
By the way, you're both going, right?

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.070
To the next Formula Stellar race.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:22.870
It's Minamoto's debut race in the Juniors after all.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.640
What?!

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.760
They won't lend it to us?!

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:27.940
Yeah.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.230
Why, Pops?!

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.850
They lent it to us last time!

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.770
I said that, too.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.550
But you see, when they have a race coming up soon,

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.350
and they say they don't have a spare machine to lend, what can you do?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.760
No...

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.950
The timing was bad.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:05.660
<i>Deeper.</i>

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.650
<i>More!</i>

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.860
<i>More!!</i>

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.990
<i>More!!!</i>

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.600
<i>Okay!</i>

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.900
<i>Yep.  Like that.</i>

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.150
Capeta?

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.200
I'm back.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.240
Welcome back.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.330
How about dinner?

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:26.680
Want me to make something?

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.580
Hey, Dad.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.210
Next week we have a parent-teacher meeting.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.900
They told me to discuss the choice of schools with you before then.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.810
I see.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:48.300
But sorry.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.770
Let's do that some other time.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.020
I'm so sleepy.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:55.300
In that case, I'll make dinner and you just eat it when you wake up.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:59.150
Hey, Capeta.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.380
What do you want to be...?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:01.190
Huh?

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.830
No.  It's nothing.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:07.620
Good night.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:15.050
<i>When I saw you out there today, I thought you should be a racer.</i>

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:19.340
<i>You should also be thinking you want to be a racer.</i>

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.440
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.520
Did I make you wait, Monami-chan?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.680
Oh, no.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:35.550
I gathered places where you could audition.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.930
We're going to prioritize places where music is their main project,

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.010
but which would you like, Monami-chan?

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.150
I've already decided.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.630
Mvex audition...

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.910
Are you graduating from the go-kart?

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.990
Oh, no.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:08.900
I heard that you got through to the final selection of the audition.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.720
Yes.  Thank you very much.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.200
So you finally caught up, huh?

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:20.310
What?  You were talking about a guy you wanted to fight.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.920
No.  I haven't caught up yet.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:32.120
But I'll take this chance no matter what.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.800
Yeah.  That's how it should be.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.180
The racing world is also a battlefield.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.210
You've come this far, so keep at it.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:40.270
Yes!

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.030
All right.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:44.200
I'm counting on you to organize the storage today.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:44.890
Yes.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:46.050
If you'll excuse me.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.650
<i>I aimed for the top of Japan but this is as far as I got.</i>

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:56.600
<i>Capeta, show me the dream I never got the chance to achieve!</i>

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:00.230
But if you could somehow, please.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.370
If you could somehow...

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.220
<i>He hung up on me.</i>

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.620
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.490
Oh yeah!  Him!

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:12.670
I am sorry,

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:18.450
but young master Momotarou is participating in a race at Oita at the moment and is not here.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:20.370
It's no good.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:21.710
Completely wiped out.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.600
<i>Hey, Capeta.</i>

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.460
<i>I'll make sure you get to practice on a formula machine this time.</i>

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.880
What was I thinking, talking over my head?!

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:34.030
I haven't changed from the time I went to look for a sponsor!

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.800
I haven't gotten any better!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.350
<i>No...  There's still another option.</i>

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:55.450
Then lastly, a word to your fans out there, if you will please.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.470
I will aim for the championship this year, too.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:01.460
Please cheer me on.

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:07.750
That was Shinkawa Hideki-san, from Formula Nippon, and a super GT driver.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.460
Thank you very much.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.660
That was a great job, Shinkawa-san.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.430
Hello, Shinkawa-san.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:16.430
Hello.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.330
That feature program was great.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:21.780
Don't you think you're being too nice to them, Shinkawa-san?

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:25.350
No.  The editor there is quite good and...

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:37.430
And so you came to me to borrow a formula machine to practice on?

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:38.550
Yes.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:42.710
If we could borrow your team's machine...

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.070
O-Of course it's impossible, right?

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.780
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:50.620
Sure.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.440
I'll lend you one.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.530
Eh?

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.050
But just the machine.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.250
The use of the circuit...

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.130
the cost for the transportation of the machine...

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.400
the cost of the gasoline...

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.950
and you'll also need mechanics.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.770
Will you be able to prepare all that?

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.390
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.440
I should have known that and still...

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.480
Andou-kun.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.910
I heard you were the one who sold Taira to Tanaka-san.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:20.370
Yes.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.770
Taira is a good driver.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.000
I think I'm lucky to have met him.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:27.880
It's thanks to you, Andou-kun.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.550
It's nothing.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:33.180
Even if I wasn't around, you would have probably met him somewhere.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.590
Capeta is incredible.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.580
Do you think so?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:43.060
As a racer, there's something I can say for sure.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:53.610
However great you are as a driver, you can't rise up to the podium by yourself.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.490
You guys are a great team.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:13.410
<i>The final selection is going to be held at the International Circuit in Shizuoka.</i>

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:20.170
<i>I'm going to do everything I can until then.</i>

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:29.580
Hey, Naomi.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:30.700
You have a visitor.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.980
Someone unexpected has come to see you.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:38.860
Hey.  It's been a while.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:44.030
Why are you here?

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.280
Minamoto.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.620
Since I lost to you in the ICA last year,

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:55.170
my aim has been to race against you again and win.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.930
I also took the audition for the FSRS this year.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.530
And I got through to the final selection.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:07.850
Please!

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.110
Introduce me to Liarize!

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.100
Your sponsor, Liarize.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:17.070
They're participating in this year's Formula Stellar, right?

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.030
I want to practice with one of their machines.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:30.580
Why should I introduce them to someone who's saying he wants to beat me?

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.170
Lift your head.

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.220
What you say is true.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.930
I'll be honest and tell you the truth.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:48.160
There's someone...

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.310
He's like a monster.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:57.020
He couldn't even connect the clutch on the first day at the school and kept stalling.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:58.830
Of course.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.500
It was his first time in a four-wheel drive.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:06.870
But in two days' time, he achieved the fastest time amongst the students during the mock race.

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.660
30.85 seconds on the Stellar Circuit!

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>Taira.</i>

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.450
I won't lose in a race.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.340
But the final selection process is based on the time attacks.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.420
I can't beat him at growth rate.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.680
I have to practice like hell!

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.890
Please!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.740
<i>I can't be worrying about how I look right now.</i>

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.400
<i>This is the only thing I can do.</i>

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:49.100
Call that place tomorrow.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.120
Minamoto.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:57.330
Thank you.

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:06.650
<b>The top at the moment is car #7, Ishihara from Team Sam's.</b>

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:12.730
<b>Following in 2nd is car #8, Minamoto, also from Sam's.</b>

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.480
<i>Shiba, huh?</i>

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:19.120
<i>He's not a bad driver.</i>

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:22.440
<i>It's not an easy thing to do.</i>

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.610
<i>To come to the one you want to beat and ask for help.</i>

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.570
<i>You have to face the humiliation.</i>

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:31.540
<i>He may get better.</i>

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.040
<i>But why?</i>

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.500
<i>Why was it Shiba?!</i>

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:41.150
<i>If you're really prepared to give up everything for racing,</i>

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:45.530
<i>couldn't it have been you coming to ask help from me, too?!</i>

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.810
Taira!

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:57.140
Minamoto!

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:58.630
<b>Whoa!</b>

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:04.310
<b>Minamoto overtakes his teammate Ishihara with his skills and rises to the top!</b>

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.660
<b>Minamoto Naomi.  He's closing in on his first win in his debut race!</b>

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.640
<b>He takes the checkered flag!</b>

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:16.700
<b>The winner is car #8.
  From Team Sam's, Minamoto Naomi!</b>

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:20.180
<b>His first race in the Formula Stellar and he wins!</b>

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.440
Minamoto is amazing.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:31.310
He won his debut race, after all.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:33.990
He was just lucky.

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.810
You're better, Ca-chan.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.030
Here.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:45.150
Sorry, I have an audition I want to go to on the same day, so I can't come and cheer you on.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.490
So this is a good luck charm.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.350
You too, Nobu.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.870
Huh?  Me too?

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:49.490
Thanks.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.600
Does this thing really work?

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:53.970
What if it takes the luck away instead?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.880
What?  What?!

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:58.200
I worked all night making those.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.550
If you don't want it, give it back!

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.550
I didn't say I didn't want it, did I?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.910
Now I don't want you to have it anymore.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:04.800
Give it back!

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.800
Fine, I'll take it.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:06.800
Give it back!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:09.130
Thank you very much.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.270
See ya, Ca-chan.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:11.170
Good luck.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:11.930
Yeah.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.970
Good luck at your audition, too, Monami.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:14.650
Yep.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.480
Bye bye!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:22.120
She sure is working hard.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.290
Yeah.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:25.940
I'm really sorry, Capeta.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:30.390
For talking smooth and promising I'd do something this time again.

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.110
I'm not cut out to be your manager.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:34.200
Really.  Don't worry about it, Nobu.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.610
No.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.290
So I've decided.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:39.500
See ya.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:50.400
<i>Nobu, Monami, thank you so much.</i>

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:54.140
A racing manager?

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.600
So that's why you changed your choice of school.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.250
But with your grades so far, it's going to be tough.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.630
I know.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.060
But I've decided.

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:08.870
To be honest, I think you should aim for some place a rank lower...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.410
I think it's okay, Tokiwa-sensei.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.940
But it's something you've decided.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.100
I won't forgive you if you take this lightly.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:16.700
Yes!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:22.150
Suzuki-san, with your grades, I think you could aim for a higher-ranking—

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.130
I'm going to become a singer.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.070
A singer?!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:29.090
Yes.  That school allows their students to participate in the entertainment business.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.670
That's why I've decided!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.640
I... I see.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.390
Sanada High School, huh?

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:39.860
That's pretty good.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.820
Well, we thought it'd be around there.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:46.560
And what would you like to be in the future, Taira-kun?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.940
I...

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:54.930
Uh...  That is...  My son would like to—

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.580
I'm asking him.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:59.170
Could you please be quiet, sir?

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:00.620
I'm sorry.

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.080
I'm going to be a racer!

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:15.870
I'm going to be the world's fastest racing driver!

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:51.730
This summer...

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:54.440
at the FSRS auditions which were held four times...

00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:58.360
35 people were dropped and
 five got through to the final selection.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:01.270
Today, the scholarship will be decided.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:02.380
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:03.410
Audition!

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:04.890
Open up the future!
